# Implementing a new instruction (LLDAR / CLLDAR) on top of the herd workflow:
# the five phases of herd-workflow.d2, with the files each commit changed placed
# beneath the phase they belong to (green), and the new litmus tests with the inputs.
# Render:   d2 --watch herd-workflow-new-instruction.d2
#           d2 --scale 2 herd-workflow-new-instruction.d2 herd-workflow-new-instruction.svg
# Phase links are pinned to commit 03c4483 of the fork. Change links point to the
# diff hunk in the GitHub commit view: cae6291 adds LLDAR (+ LA annotation, bob
# edge), 03c4483 adds CLLDAR. Format: commit/<sha>#diff-<sha256(path)>R<line>.

vars: {
  d2-config: {
    layout-engine: elk
  }
}

direction: right

classes: {
  phase: {
    grid-columns: 1
    vertical-gap: 24
    style: {
      fill: "#e8f0fe"
      stroke: "#3b6fd8"
      stroke-width: 2
      border-radius: 10
      font-size: 24
      bold: true
    }
  }
  structs: {
    label: ""
    grid-columns: 2
    horizontal-gap: 16
    vertical-gap: 12
    style: {
      fill: transparent
      stroke: transparent
    }
  }
  struct: {
    shape: rectangle
    width: 340
    style: {
      fill: "#fff8e6"
      stroke: "#8a6d1f"
      border-radius: 4
      font-size: 14
    }
  }
  examples: {
    shape: rectangle
    style: {
      fill: transparent
      stroke: transparent
      font-size: 14
    }
  }
  io: {
    style: {
      fill: "#ffffff"
      stroke: "#5b6475"
    }
  }
  changes: {
    shape: rectangle
    style: {
      fill: "#e9f7ec"
      stroke: "#2e8b57"
      stroke-width: 2
      border-radius: 10
      font-size: 14
    }
  }
  handoff: {
    style: {
      stroke: "#3b6fd8"
      stroke-width: 2
      font-size: 14
    }
  }
}

# Grid layout: row 1 is the workflow, row 2 the changes beneath each phase.
workflow: {
  label: ""
  # rows first: cells fill row by row (row 1 phases, row 2 changes)
  grid-rows: 2
  grid-columns: 6
  horizontal-gap: 120
  vertical-gap: 40
  style: {fill: transparent; stroke: transparent}

  # ───────────────────────── Inputs ─────────────────────────

  inputs: {
    label: ""
    grid-rows: 2
    vertical-gap: 40
    style: {fill: transparent; stroke: transparent}

    litmus: "litmus test\n(.litmus)" {shape: page; class: io}
    cat: "memory model\n(.cat)" {shape: page; class: io}
  }

  # ───────────────────────── 1 · Parsing ─────────────────────────

  parsing: "1 · Parsing" {
    class: phase

    desc: |md
      menhir-parsers transform litmus test into the internal representations
      [**test_herd**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/test_herd.mli#L20) and cat-model [**model**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/model.mli#L23):

      1. [**select**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/parseTest.ml#L88) architecture ([**Archs.parse**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/lib/Archs.ml#L48))
         from the test's architecture string
      2. [**select**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/parseTest.ml#L168) the architecture's litmus parser
      3. [**parses**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/runTest.ml#L65) the program (it becomes a [**map**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/archExtra_herd.ml#L83)
         addr/label → instruction-list)
    |

    structs: {
      class: structs
      test: |md
        [**test_herd.mli**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/test_herd.mli#L20) and [**archExtra_herd.ml**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/archExtra_herd.ml#L83) \
        internal representation \
        of the litmus program
      | {class: struct}
      parser: |md
        [**XXXParser.mly**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/lib/AArch64Parser.mly) \
        architecture grammar & \
        token-to-object translation
      | {class: struct}
    }

    examples: |md
      *Examples:* [**LDR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/lib/AArch64Parser.mly#L700) · [**CBZ**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/lib/AArch64Parser.mly#L693)
    | {class: examples}
  }

  # ───────────────────────── 2 · Candidates ─────────────────────────

  candidates: "2 · Construct Candidate Event Structures" {
    class: phase

    desc: |md
      [**glommed_event_structures**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/mem.ml#L342) generates potential control-flow-fixed
      event structures, collecting thread-local constraints for register values.
      It generates only iico-edges and po-indices (effectively po-edges). No rf/co edges yet.

      1. [**translates**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/AArch64Sem.ml#L4120) instructions into constraint lists & event structures
         according to its semantics
      2. [**stitches**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/mem.ml#L652) them together with the
         [**code monad**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/eventsMonad.ml#L1125) (generating po-indices)
    |

    structs: {
      class: structs
      drivers: |md
        [**runTest.ml**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/runTest.ml) and [**top_herd.ml**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/top_herd.ml) \
        dispatch and oversight \
        to run a test
      | {class: struct}
      monad: |md
        [**monad.mli**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/monad.mli) and [**eventsMonad.ml**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/eventsMonad.ml) \
        providing binders for the construction \
        of potential event structures
      | {class: struct}
      sem: |md
        [**XXXSem.ml**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/AArch64Sem.ml) \
        uses the binders to translate every \
        instruction into event structures \
        with iico-edges
      | {class: struct}
      es: |md
        [**eventStructure**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/event.ml#L215) \
        event structures. holds instruction internal \
        iico-edges & beyond-instruction po-edges. \
        Every event has an action with a return type
      | {class: struct}
    }

    examples: |md
      *Examples:* [**LDR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/AArch64Sem.ml#L4221) · [**CBZ**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/AArch64Sem.ml#L4195)
    | {class: examples}
  }

  # ───────────────────────── 3 · Concrete ─────────────────────────

  concrete: "3 · Generate Concrete Event Structures" {
    class: phase

    desc: |md
      [**exec_iter**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/top_herd.ml#L493) takes a potential event structure and iterates over
      concrete instantiations of it with [**iter_rfms**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/top_herd.ml#L310) to fix readfrom relations:

      1. [**solve**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/mem.ml#L1092) its thread-local constraints.
         discard the potential event structure if not possible.
      2. [**enumerate**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/mem.ml#L1379) memory rf relations and their constraints
         (equality of written and read value).
      3. [**solve**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/mem.ml#L1416) each rf relation's constraints.
         discard a rf relation if not possible.
      4. [**partially sets co**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/mem.ml#L2244): (final) writes per location
         and initial writes come first.
    |

    structs: {
      class: structs
      drivers: |md
        [**runTest.ml**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/runTest.ml) and [**top_herd.ml**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/top_herd.ml) \
        dispatch and oversight \
        to run a test
      | {class: struct}
      rfmap: |md
        [**rfmap**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/semExtra.ml#L134) \
        keeps track of which event obtained its value \
        from which other event (both for registers/memory)
      | {class: struct}
      conc: |md
        [**concrete**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/semExtra.ml#L170) \
        event structure + rfmap \
        \+ final writes (inside rfmap)
      | {class: struct}
    }
  }

  # ───────────────────────── 4 · Checking ─────────────────────────

  checking: "4 · Check Concrete Event Structures" {
    class: phase

    desc: |md
      an interpreter executing the CAT-model line-by-line on the concrete
      event structure ([**call_model**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/top_herd.ml#L496)) to identify whether the concrete
      event structure is possible:

      1. [**enumerate**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/libdir/cross.cat#L28) possible co orders and fork further evaluation for each
      2. [**initialise**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/lib/interpreter.ml#L2738) env with base relations (po, rf, co, iico-data, iico-ctrl)
      3. [**execute**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/lib/interpreter.ml#L1262) each line of the model
      4. [**collects**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/top_herd.ml#L496) the concrete event structures, whether rejected or
         allowed and whether they satisfy postcondition or not.
    |

    structs: {
      class: structs
      model: |md
        [**model.mli**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/model.mli#L23) \
        internal representation \
        of the cat-model
      | {class: struct}
      ast: |md
        [**AST.mli**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/lib/AST.mli#L117) \
        Internal representation \
        of parsed CAT-Syntax
      | {class: struct}
      st: |md
        [**st**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/lib/interpreter.ml#L574) \
        state of cat interpreter, containing [**env**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/lib/interpreter.ml#L324), \
        the map from var-names to their [**values**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/lib/interpreter.ml#L309) (relations)
      | {class: struct}
      count: |md
        [**Count.t**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/top_herd.ml#L268) \
        collects the results
      | {class: struct}
    }

    examples: |md
      *Examples:* [**dependency-ordered-before**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/libdir/aarch64hwreqs.cat#L93) · [**dtrm**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/libdir/aarch64deps.cat#L61) · [**aarch64 constraints**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/libdir/aarch64.cat#L160)
    | {class: examples}
  }

  # ───────────────────────── 5 · Printing ─────────────────────────

  printing: "5 · Print Results" {
    class: phase

    desc: |md
      [**outputs**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/top_herd.ml#L164) the stats collected:

      - Allowed (exists-query) / Forbidden (~exists) / Required (forall)
      - States: the final states reached by allowed event structures
        (restricted to variables in constraint)
      - Ok / No: whether postcondition is true or false
      - Positive / Negative: count of event structures with true / false postcondition
    |

    structs: {
      class: structs
      stats: |md
        [**stats**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/blob/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0/herd/top_herd.mli#L39) \
        collected stats during the run
      | {class: struct}
    }
  }

  # ───────────────────────── Row 2: changes ─────────────────────────
  # (declared in grid order; the empty cells keep the columns aligned)
  inputs_changes: |md
    **Write Litmus tests to check intended behaviour**

    1. LLDAR
       - test for ordering ([**MP+rel+LLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-703014ffa7c91dda91ccc4ef42953c24668cd4d31d182f1d9590d79fa2b114c1R1))
       - test for non-ordering with later memory instruction
         ([**MP+rel+LLDAR-fail**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-ba6c4ce62159c99b1487bc99a0e1a5bdc6ea508e7688aa2a90975c5fda101463R1))
    2. CLLDAR
       - test for ordering ([**MP+rel+CLLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-e7cf9486ace110b1585c5bab8eac64c890bb98defa07d338c30b9316e70b82e9R1))
       - test for non-ordering with later memory instruction
         ([**MP+rel+CLLDAR-fail**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-609655c09c0f39317bb981754e9152c589defcd7ed6830a596a78ef13859f1abR1))
  | {class: changes}

  parsing_changes: |md
    **Parsing**

    1. Introduce the instruction in AArch64Base.ml
       ([**LLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-87c59e17c30b4a451f5222d06442d112d13bc5348634c3664db613942d49cf4cR1254) reuses the LDAR struct, [**CLLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-87c59e17c30b4a451f5222d06442d112d13bc5348634c3664db613942d49cf4cR1446))
    2. Create them in menhir grammar
       ([**LLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-bf4e9be18ed9e7f82da1b4d172d634df793e6963c2f38955e52dfd5e6307d814R748), [**CLLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-bf4e9be18ed9e7f82da1b4d172d634df793e6963c2f38955e52dfd5e6307d814R750))
  | {class: changes}

  candidates_changes: |md
    **Instruction semantics**

    1. Encode instruction semantics using the monad binders
       ([**CLLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-f2a12c2f4bc2d0aa25e415c57b77bfe6c912fb2a2b841e23fc03922cdeafb1ecR4241))
    2. Write integration test ([**LLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-7e3f509470844ba0a9291375ffa0e902741549ad6a7f6dfbc671b68a4f83515aR1), [**CLLDAR**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/03c448313911e11ae29c2171fe4b6409616f0af0#diff-3633e9d5635759e4e77a9a37a43f3b06cb1fb62330e06491d4a10f03a6f7e403R1))
  | {class: changes}

  concrete_changes: {label: ""; style: {fill: transparent; stroke: transparent}}

  checking_changes: |md
    **Cat semantics**

    1. Introduce a new cat annotation: LA (limited acquire)
       ([**LA**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-05772012f80903bb4d4dc5c9998c03e96d3a69e1f313be7d2e138a89bb93f4d3R19))
    2. Introduce limited-acquire edges to the CAT model
       ([**bob**](https://github.com/svdwall/herdtools7/commit/cae6291049c4e2d52cb199b785d7f510315243e5#diff-48de46133a6939978d62812c18eb510164eab583412b943fb1674f9d2cb10452R139))
  | {class: changes}

  printing_changes: {label: ""; style: {fill: transparent; stroke: transparent}}

  # ───────────────────────── Hand-offs ─────────────────────────

  inputs.litmus -> parsing
  inputs.cat -> parsing
  parsing -> candidates: "Test_herd.t" {class: handoff}
  candidates -> concrete: "candidates\n+ constraints" {class: handoff}
  concrete -> checking: "each S.concrete" {class: handoff}
  checking -> printing: "Count.t → stats" {class: handoff}
}
